{"id":10,"title":"Laws of Exponents & Roots — Fundamentals","subject":"algebra","sections":[{"id":"power-theory","title":"Eight guided questions","kind":"learn","steps":[{"kind":"video","id":"powers-techniques","minutes":2.5,"title":"Exponents & Roots — Techniques"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-248","stem":"\\(\\frac{{9}^{6} \\cdot  {8}^{-2}}{{3}^{8} \\cdot  {4}^{-2}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\({3}^{4} \\cdot  {2}^{-2}\\)","\\({3}^{-2} \\cdot  {2}^{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{{2}^{2}}{{3}^{4}}\\)","\\(\\frac{{3}^{4}}{{2}^{5}}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Write every base as a prime: \\(9^6=(3^2)^6=3^{12}\\), \\(8^{-2}=(2^3)^{-2}=2^{-6}\\), \\(4^{-2}=(2^2)^{-2}=2^{-4}\\).","The fraction becomes \\(\\frac{3^{12}\\cdot2^{-6}}{3^8\\cdot2^{-4}}=3^{12-8}\\cdot2^{-6-(-4)}=3^4\\cdot2^{-2}\\)."],"number":1},{"kind":"video","id":"solve-q-248","minutes":1.5,"solution":true,"questionId":"q-248","title":"Worked solution · Question 1"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-249","stem":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{27} + \\sqrt{27}}{\\sqrt{48} - \\sqrt{12}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(5\\,\\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(\\sqrt{2}\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(9\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Simplify each root: \\(\\sqrt{27}=3\\sqrt3\\), \\(\\sqrt{48}=4\\sqrt3\\), \\(\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt3\\).","Numerator: \\(3\\sqrt3+3\\sqrt3=6\\sqrt3\\). Denominator: \\(4\\sqrt3-2\\sqrt3=2\\sqrt3\\).","\\(\\frac{6\\sqrt3}{2\\sqrt3}=3\\)."],"number":2},{"kind":"video","id":"solve-q-249","minutes":1.3,"solution":true,"questionId":"q-249","title":"Worked solution · Question 2"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-250","stem":"Given: \\({4}^{2\\,x} = {\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)}^{4 - 2\\,x}\\)\n\\(x = ?\\)","choices":["\\(4\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(5\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Write both sides with base 2: \\(4^{2x}=(2^2)^{2x}=2^{4x}\\), and \\(\\frac18=2^{-3}\\), so \\(\\left(\\frac18\\right)^{4-2x}=2^{-3(4-2x)}=2^{-12+6x}\\).","Equal bases, so the exponents are equal: \\(4x=-12+6x\\). Therefore \\(2x=12\\) and \\(x=6\\)."],"number":3},{"kind":"video","id":"solve-q-250","minutes":1.5,"solution":true,"questionId":"q-250","title":"Worked solution · Question 3"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-251","stem":"Given: \\(\\sqrt{x-7}=3\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(4\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(16\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Square both sides: \\(x-7=9\\), so \\(x=16\\).","Check: \\(\\sqrt{16-7}=\\sqrt9=3\\) ✓."],"number":4},{"kind":"video","id":"solve-q-251","minutes":0.4,"solution":true,"questionId":"q-251","title":"Worked solution · Question 4"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-252","stem":"Given:\n\\(\\begin{cases} x\\ne0 \\\\ x\\sqrt5=5\\sqrt x \\end{cases}\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(25\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(\\sqrt{5}\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Square both sides: \\((x\\sqrt5)^2=(5\\sqrt x)^2\\), so \\(5x^2=25x\\).","Divide by 5: \\(x^2=5x\\). Since \\(x\\ne0\\), divide by \\(x\\): \\(x=5\\).","Check: \\(5\\sqrt5=5\\sqrt5\\) ✓.","If \\(x\\ne0\\) were not given, factor instead of dividing: \\(x(x-5)=0\\), so \\(x=0\\) or \\(x=5\\)."],"number":5},{"kind":"video","id":"solve-q-252","minutes":1.1,"solution":true,"questionId":"q-252","title":"Worked solution · Question 5"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-01","stem":"Given: \\(\\sqrt{2x+3}=x\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(-1\\)","\\(1\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(-1\\) or \\(3\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["The root is never negative, so \\(x\\ge0\\).","Square both sides: \\(2x+3=x^2\\), so \\(x^2-2x-3=0\\) and \\((x-3)(x+1)=0\\): \\(x=3\\) or \\(x=-1\\).","Check in the original: \\(x=3\\): \\(\\sqrt9=3\\) ✓. \\(x=-1\\): \\(\\sqrt1=1\\ne-1\\) ✗ (fake solution).","Only \\(x=3\\). Faster: try the choices — \\(-1\\) fails, \\(1\\) fails (\\(\\sqrt5\\ne1\\)), \\(3\\) works."],"number":6},{"kind":"video","id":"solve-q-r26-t10-01","minutes":1.1,"solution":true,"questionId":"q-r26-t10-01","title":"Worked solution · Question 6"},{"kind":"video","id":"r26-t10-power-traps","minutes":0.9,"title":"Exponent Traps — Sums of Powers"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-02","stem":"\\(2^{10}+2^{10}+2^{10}+2^{10}=?\\)","choices":["\\(8^{10}\\)","\\(2^{12}\\)","\\(2^{40}\\)","\\(8^{40}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Four equal powers: \\(2^{10}+2^{10}+2^{10}+2^{10}=4\\cdot2^{10}\\).","\\(4=2^2\\), so \\(4\\cdot2^{10}=2^2\\cdot2^{10}=2^{12}\\).","Adding the exponents (\\(2^{40}\\)) or adding the bases (\\(8^{10}\\)) is the trap: there is no law for adding powers."],"number":7},{"kind":"video","id":"solve-q-r26-t10-02","minutes":0.9,"solution":true,"questionId":"q-r26-t10-02","title":"Worked solution · Question 7"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-03","stem":"Given: \\(3^{x+2}-3^x=72\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(1\\)","\\(2\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(4\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Take out the smallest power: \\(3^{x+2}-3^x=3^x(3^2-1)=8\\cdot3^x\\).","\\(8\\cdot3^x=72\\), so \\(3^x=9=3^2\\) and \\(x=2\\).","Check: \\(3^4-3^2=81-9=72\\) ✓."],"number":8},{"kind":"video","id":"solve-q-r26-t10-03","minutes":0.8,"solution":true,"questionId":"q-r26-t10-03","title":"Worked solution · Question 8"},{"kind":"card","id":"mem-r26-t10-techniques","title":"Exponent and root techniques","intro":"The methods of this topic, each with one example.","tables":[{"title":"Techniques","head":["Situation","Method","Example"],"rows":[["Number over a root","ignore the root, then put it back","\\(\\frac6{\\sqrt3}=2\\sqrt3\\)"],["Different bases","write every base as the smallest prime","\\(8^4=2^{12}=16^3\\)"],["Negative exponent","flip the base","\\(3^4\\cdot2^{-3}=\\frac{3^4}{2^3}\\)"],["Adding roots","split, or take a common factor","\\(\\sqrt8+\\sqrt{18}=5\\sqrt2\\)"],["Equal powers added","count the copies","\\(2^x+2^x=2\\cdot2^x=2^{x+1}\\)"],["Same base, different exponents","take out the smallest power","\\(2^{x+2}-2^x=3\\cdot2^x\\)"],["Same exponent","multiply the bases","\\(2^x\\cdot5^x=10^x\\)"],["Power equation","equal bases, then equal exponents","\\(3^{2x-1}=3^3\\Rightarrow x=2\\)"],["Root equation","square, solve, check in the original","\\(\\sqrt{x+2}=x\\Rightarrow x=2\\) only"]]}],"tips":["Trap: \\(2^x+2^x\\ne4^x\\). Check with \\(x=3\\): \\(8+8=16\\), but \\(4^3=64\\).","Mixed bases in a fraction? Pair the families: \\(\\frac{9^6\\cdot8^{-2}}{3^8\\cdot4^{-2}}=\\frac{9^6}{3^8}\\cdot\\left(\\frac84\\right)^{-2}\\).","Four choices? Try them. It is often faster, and it throws out fake solutions of root equations.","If \\(x\\ne0\\) is NOT given, factor — don't divide by \\(x\\): \\(x^2=5x\\Rightarrow x(x-5)=0\\).","Expression choices? Choose an easy value (\\(x=2\\) or \\(x=3\\)). If two choices match, try another number."]},{"kind":"video","id":"r26-t10-summary","minutes":2.6,"title":"Exponents & Roots — Summary"}]},{"id":"unit-t10-2","title":"Expressions and equations","kind":"practice","steps":[{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-2-1","stem":"\\(\\frac{3^7}{3^4}=?\\)","choices":["\\(3\\)","\\(9\\)","\\(81\\)","\\(27\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Same base: subtract the exponents. \\(\\frac{3^7}{3^4}=3^{7-4}=3^3=27\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-254","stem":"\\({3}^{2} \\cdot  {9}^{3} = ?\\)","choices":["\\({3}^{8}\\)","\\({3}^{7}\\)","\\({3}^{6}\\)","\\({3}^{5}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["\\(9^3=(3^2)^3=3^6\\), so \\(3^2\\cdot3^6=3^{2+6}=3^8\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-2-3","stem":"Given: \\(3^{x+1}=3^5\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(3\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(12\\)","\\(4\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Equal bases, so the exponents are equal: \\(x+1=5\\). Therefore \\(x=4\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-256","stem":"Given: \\(7^2=7^{x+6}\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(-4\\)","\\(-1\\)","\\(4\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Equal bases, so the exponents are equal: \\(x+6=2\\). Therefore \\(x=-4\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-262","stem":"\\(\\sqrt{28} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(7\\,\\sqrt{2}\\)","\\(2\\,\\sqrt{7}\\)","\\(4\\,\\sqrt{7}\\)","\\(2\\,\\sqrt{14}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Pull out the largest square: \\(28=4\\cdot7\\), so \\(\\sqrt{28}=\\sqrt4\\cdot\\sqrt7=2\\sqrt7\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-264","stem":"\\(\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{27} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(3\\,\\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(4\\,\\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(2\\,\\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(5\\,\\sqrt{3}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["\\(\\sqrt{27}=\\sqrt9\\cdot\\sqrt3=3\\sqrt3\\).","\\(\\sqrt3+3\\sqrt3=4\\sqrt3\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-265","stem":"\\(\\sqrt{80} - \\sqrt{20} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(4\\,\\sqrt{5}\\)","\\(3\\,\\sqrt{5}\\)","\\(2\\,\\sqrt{5}\\)","\\(2\\,\\sqrt{15}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["\\(\\sqrt{80}=\\sqrt{16}\\cdot\\sqrt5=4\\sqrt5\\) and \\(\\sqrt{20}=\\sqrt4\\cdot\\sqrt5=2\\sqrt5\\).","\\(4\\sqrt5-2\\sqrt5=2\\sqrt5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-263","stem":"\\(\\sqrt{63}=?\\)","choices":["\\(4\\,\\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(3\\,\\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(2\\,\\sqrt{7}\\)","\\(3\\,\\sqrt{7}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["\\(63=9\\cdot7\\), therefore \\(\\sqrt{63}=\\sqrt9\\cdot\\sqrt7=3\\sqrt7\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-2-7","stem":"\\(\\sqrt{72}+\\sqrt{18}=?\\)","choices":["\\(9\\sqrt2\\)","\\(\\sqrt{90}\\)","\\(10\\sqrt2\\)","\\(8\\sqrt2\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["\\(\\sqrt{72}=\\sqrt{36}\\cdot\\sqrt2=6\\sqrt2\\) and \\(\\sqrt{18}=\\sqrt9\\cdot\\sqrt2=3\\sqrt2\\).","\\(6\\sqrt2+3\\sqrt2=9\\sqrt2\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-260","stem":"\\(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(2\\,\\sqrt{5}\\)","\\(5\\,\\sqrt{5}\\)","\\(2\\,\\sqrt{2}\\)","\\(5\\,\\sqrt{2}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Ignore the root: \\(10\\div5=2\\). Put the root back on the answer: \\(2\\sqrt5\\).","Why it works: \\(10=2\\cdot\\sqrt5\\cdot\\sqrt5\\), so \\(\\frac{2\\cdot\\sqrt5\\cdot\\sqrt5}{\\sqrt5}=2\\sqrt5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-261","stem":"\\(\\frac{5\\,\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{15}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(5\\)","\\(\\sqrt{5}\\)","\\(\\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Split the denominator: \\(\\sqrt{15}=\\sqrt3\\cdot\\sqrt5\\).","Cancel \\(\\sqrt3\\): \\(\\frac{5\\sqrt3}{\\sqrt3\\cdot\\sqrt5}=\\frac5{\\sqrt5}\\).","Number over a root: \\(5\\div5=1\\), then put the root back: \\(\\sqrt5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-257","stem":"Given: \\(2^8=4^{x-1}\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(8\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(2\\)","\\(5\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["\\(4=2^2\\), so \\(4^{x-1}=2^{2(x-1)}=2^{2x-2}\\).","Equal exponents: \\(2x-2=8\\), so \\(2x=10\\) and \\(x=5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-258","stem":"Given: \\(8^5=4^4\\cdot2^x\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(4\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(2\\)","\\(7\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Base 2 everywhere: \\(8^5=2^{15}\\) and \\(4^4=2^8\\).","\\(2^{15}=2^8\\cdot2^x=2^{8+x}\\), so \\(8+x=15\\) and \\(x=7\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-259","stem":"Given: \\(\\left(\\frac15\\right)^3=5^{x-7}\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(4\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(2\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["\\(\\frac15=5^{-1}\\), so \\(\\left(\\frac15\\right)^3=5^{-3}\\).","Equal exponents: \\(x-7=-3\\), so \\(x=4\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-253","stem":"\\(\\frac{{3}^{5}}{{15}^{2}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{27}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{9}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{27}{25}\\)","\\(\\frac{9}{25}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["\\(15^2=(3\\cdot5)^2=3^2\\cdot5^2\\).","\\(\\frac{3^5}{3^2\\cdot5^2}=\\frac{3^3}{5^2}=\\frac{27}{25}\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-255","stem":"\\(\\frac{{16}^{3} \\cdot  {8}^{2}}{{4}^{4} \\cdot  {2}^{6}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\({2}^{4}\\)","\\({2}^{3}\\)","\\({2}^{6}\\)","\\({2}^{5}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["All bases are powers of 2: \\(16^3=2^{12}\\), \\(8^2=2^6\\), \\(4^4=2^8\\).","Numerator: \\(2^{12}\\cdot2^6=2^{18}\\). Denominator: \\(2^8\\cdot2^6=2^{14}\\).","\\(\\frac{2^{18}}{2^{14}}=2^{18-14}=2^4\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-2-4","stem":"\\(3^{-3}+3^{-2}=?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{243}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{27}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{9}\\)","\\(\\frac{4}{27}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["\\(3^{-3}=\\frac1{27}\\) and \\(3^{-2}=\\frac19=\\frac3{27}\\).","\\(\\frac1{27}+\\frac3{27}=\\frac4{27}\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-2-5","stem":"Given: \\(x\\ne0\\)\n\\(\\frac{(3x)^3}{9x^2}=?\\)","choices":["\\(x\\)","\\(27x\\)","\\(3x\\)","\\(3x^2\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["\\((3x)^3=27x^3\\).","\\(\\frac{27x^3}{9x^2}=\\frac{27}{9}\\cdot x^{3-2}=3x\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-2-2","stem":"\\(64^{\\frac23}=?\\)","choices":["\\(8\\)","\\(48\\)","\\(16\\)","\\(4\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["\\(64^{\\frac23}=\\left(\\sqrt[3]{64}\\right)^2=4^2=16\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-2-6","stem":"Which is greater: \\(2^{12}\\) or \\(4^5\\)?","choices":["They are equal","It cannot be determined from the information given.","The first power","The second power"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Same base: \\(4^5=(2^2)^5=2^{10}\\).","\\(2^{12}>2^{10}\\), therefore the first power, \\(2^{12}\\), is greater."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-266","stem":"Given: \\(\\sqrt{2\\,x + 9} = 5\\)\n\\(x = ?\\)","choices":["\\(8\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(5\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Square both sides: \\(2x+9=25\\), so \\(2x=16\\) and \\(x=8\\).","Check: \\(\\sqrt{2\\cdot8+9}=\\sqrt{25}=5\\) ✓."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-267","stem":"Given: \\(\\sqrt{4\\,x + 6} = \\sqrt{70}\\)\n\\(x = ?\\)","choices":["\\(14\\)","\\(13\\)","\\(16\\)","\\(15\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Square both sides: \\(4x+6=70\\), so \\(4x=64\\) and \\(x=16\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-06","stem":"\\(5^x+5^x+5^x+5^x+5^x=?\\)","choices":["\\(25^x\\)","\\(5^{5x}\\)","\\(5^{x+1}\\)","\\(25^{5x}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Five equal powers: \\(5^x+5^x+5^x+5^x+5^x=5\\cdot5^x=5^1\\cdot5^x=5^{x+1}\\).","If you check with a number, avoid \\(x=1\\) (then \\(25^x=25\\) too). With \\(x=2\\): \\(5\\cdot25=125=5^3\\), while \\(25^2=625\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-08","stem":"Given: \\(4^x\\cdot25^x=10^6\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(2\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(12\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Same exponent, so multiply the bases: \\(4^x\\cdot25^x=100^x\\).","\\(100^x=(10^2)^x=10^{2x}\\), so \\(2x=6\\) and \\(x=3\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-07","stem":"Given: \\(0.2^x=25\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(2\\)","\\(-2\\)","\\(\\frac12\\)","\\(-\\frac12\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["\\(0.2=\\frac15=5^{-1}\\), so \\(0.2^x=5^{-x}\\). Also \\(25=5^2\\).","Equal exponents: \\(-x=2\\), so \\(x=-2\\).","Check: \\(0.2^{-2}=5^2=25\\) ✓."]}]},{"id":"unit-t10-3","title":"Mixed practice","kind":"practice","steps":[{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-3-1","stem":"\\(\\frac{4^8}{4^5}=?\\)","choices":["\\(64\\)","\\(4\\)","\\(16\\)","\\(256\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Same base: subtract the exponents. \\(\\frac{4^8}{4^5}=4^{8-5}=4^3=64\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-276","stem":"\\(7^x\\cdot7^{-x}=?\\)","choices":["\\(49\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{7}\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Add the exponents: \\(x+(-x)=0\\), so the product is \\(7^0=1\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-277","stem":"Given: \\(x=y=8\\)\n\\(x^{y-x}\\cdot y^{x-y}=?\\)","choices":["\\(64\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(0\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Since \\(x=y=8\\), both exponents are zero: \\(y-x=8-8=0\\) and \\(x-y=8-8=0\\).","Therefore the product is \\(8^0\\cdot8^0=1\\cdot1=1\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-3-3","stem":"Given: \\(3^{x+1}=3^6\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(15\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(4\\)","\\(6\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Equal bases, so the exponents are equal: \\(x+1=6\\). Therefore \\(x=5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-283","stem":"\\(\\sqrt{98}=?\\)","choices":["\\(7\\,\\sqrt{2}\\)","\\(2\\,\\sqrt{7}\\)","\\(7\\,\\sqrt{7}\\)","\\(4\\,\\sqrt{6}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["\\(98=49\\cdot2\\), therefore \\(\\sqrt{98}=\\sqrt{49}\\cdot\\sqrt2=7\\sqrt2\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-274","stem":"Given: \\({2}^{n + 1} = 64\\)\n\\(n = ?\\)","choices":["\\(6\\)","\\(2\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(5\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["\\(64=2^6\\), so \\(n+1=6\\) and \\(n=5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-3-7","stem":"\\(\\sqrt{98}+\\sqrt{32}=?\\)","choices":["\\(11\\sqrt2\\)","\\(\\sqrt{130}\\)","\\(12\\sqrt2\\)","\\(10\\sqrt2\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["\\(\\sqrt{98}=\\sqrt{49}\\cdot\\sqrt2=7\\sqrt2\\) and \\(\\sqrt{32}=\\sqrt{16}\\cdot\\sqrt2=4\\sqrt2\\).","\\(7\\sqrt2+4\\sqrt2=11\\sqrt2\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-268","stem":"Given: \\(x>0\\)\n\\(x^{x+3}\\cdot x^{-x-2}=?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac1x\\)","\\(x\\)","\\(0\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Same base: add the exponents. \\((x+3)+(-x-2)=1\\), so the product is \\(x^1=x\\).","Faster: choose an easy value, \\(x=2\\): \\(2^5\\cdot2^{-4}=2^1=2\\). Only choice (2) gives \\(2\\) (\\(\\frac1x=\\frac12\\), and the others are \\(0\\) and \\(1\\))."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-270","stem":"Given: \\(a>0\\)\n\\(\\frac{a^{a+2}}{a^2}=?\\)","choices":["\\({a}^{a + 4}\\)","\\({\\left(a + 2\\right)}^{a}\\)","\\({a}^{a}\\)","\\(a + 2\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Same base: subtract the exponents. \\(\\frac{a^{a+2}}{a^2}=a^{a+2-2}=a^a\\).","With easy values: \\(a=2\\) gives \\(\\frac{2^4}{2^2}=4\\), but two choices give \\(4\\) (\\(a^a\\) and \\(a+2\\)). Try another number: \\(a=3\\) gives \\(\\frac{3^5}{3^2}=27\\), and only \\(a^a=27\\) fits."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-278","stem":"Given: \\(a>0\\) and \\(c>0\\)\n\\(\\frac{5a^8c^6}{a^2c^3}=?\\)","choices":["\\(5\\,{a}^{4}{c}^{2}\\)","\\(5\\,{a}^{6}{c}^{3}\\)","\\(5\\,{a}^{8}{c}^{6}\\)","\\(5\\,{a}^{4}{c}^{3}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Handle each base on its own and subtract the exponents: \\(a^{8-2}=a^6\\) and \\(c^{6-3}=c^3\\).","The 5 does not change: \\(5a^6c^3\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-279","stem":"\\((3^4)^3\\cdot3^{-14}=?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{9}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)","\\(-9\\)","\\(-3\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["\\((3^4)^3=3^{12}\\).","\\(3^{12}\\cdot3^{-14}=3^{-2}=\\frac1{3^2}=\\frac19\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-3-4","stem":"\\(4^{-3}+4^{-2}=?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{1024}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{64}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\)","\\(\\frac{5}{64}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["\\(4^{-3}=\\frac1{64}\\) and \\(4^{-2}=\\frac1{16}=\\frac4{64}\\).","\\(\\frac1{64}+\\frac4{64}=\\frac5{64}\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-3-5","stem":"Given: \\(x\\ne0\\)\n\\(\\frac{(4x)^3}{16x^2}=?\\)","choices":["\\(x\\)","\\(64x\\)","\\(4x\\)","\\(4x^2\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["\\((4x)^3=64x^3\\).","\\(\\frac{64x^3}{16x^2}=\\frac{64}{16}\\cdot x^{3-2}=4x\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-3-2","stem":"\\(125^{\\frac23}=?\\)","choices":["\\(75\\)","\\(25\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(10\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["\\(125^{\\frac23}=\\left(\\sqrt[3]{125}\\right)^2=5^2=25\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t10-3-6","stem":"Which is greater: \\(2^{14}\\) or \\(4^6\\)?","choices":["It cannot be determined from the information given.","The first power","The second power","They are equal"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Same base: \\(4^6=(2^2)^6=2^{12}\\).","\\(2^{14}>2^{12}\\), therefore the first power, \\(2^{14}\\), is greater."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-272","stem":"\\(\\frac{{9}^{3} \\cdot  {3}^{4}}{81} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(3\\)","\\({3}^{5}\\)","\\({3}^{6}\\)","\\({3}^{10}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Base 3 everywhere: \\(9^3=3^6\\) and \\(81=3^4\\).","\\(\\frac{3^6\\cdot3^4}{3^4}=3^6\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-271","stem":"\\({16}^{x} \\cdot  {4}^{x} \\cdot  {2}^{x} = ?\\)","choices":["\\({2}^{4\\,x}\\)","\\({2}^{5\\,x}\\)","\\({2}^{7\\,x}\\)","\\({4}^{3\\,x}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Write every base as a power of 2: \\(16^x=2^{4x}\\), \\(4^x=2^{2x}\\).","Add the exponents: \\(4x+2x+x=7x\\), so the product is \\(2^{7x}\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-273","stem":"\\({36}^{4} = ?\\)","choices":["\\({216}^{2}\\)","\\({\\left({6}^{2}\\right)}^{8}\\)","\\({72}^{2}\\)","\\({6}^{8}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["\\(36=6^2\\), so \\(36^4=(6^2)^4=6^8\\).","The others: \\(216^2=(6^3)^2=6^6\\), \\((6^2)^8=6^{16}\\), and \\(72^2=(2\\cdot36)^2=4\\cdot6^4\\). None of them is \\(6^8\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-269","stem":"Given: \\(\\sqrt{x^2}=5\\). Which of the following could be the value of \\(x\\)?","choices":["\\(25\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{5}\\)","\\(-5\\)","\\(-1\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["\\(\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|\\), so \\(|x|=5\\): \\(x=5\\) or \\(x=-5\\).","Only \\(-5\\) is among the choices."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-280","stem":"Given: \\(x>0\\)\n\\(x^{\\frac34}\\cdot x^{\\frac43}=?\\)","choices":["\\(1\\)","\\(x\\)","\\(x^{\\frac{12}{25}}\\)","\\(x^{\\frac{25}{12}}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Same base: add the exponents. \\(\\frac34+\\frac43=\\frac9{12}+\\frac{16}{12}=\\frac{25}{12}\\).","So the product is \\(x^{\\frac{25}{12}}\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-275","stem":"\\({\\left({5}^{-\\sqrt{3}}\\right)}^{-\\sqrt{3}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\({5}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\)","\\({25}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(125\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Power of a power: multiply the exponents. \\((-\\sqrt3)\\cdot(-\\sqrt3)=(\\sqrt3)^2=3\\).","So the expression is \\(5^3=125\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-282","stem":"Given: \\(x + y + z = 5\\)\n\\({3}^{x} \\cdot  {3}^{y} \\cdot  {3}^{z} = ?\\)","choices":["It cannot be determined from the information given.","\\(15\\)","\\(125\\)","\\(243\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["\\(3^x\\cdot3^y\\cdot3^z=3^{x+y+z}=3^5=243\\).","We do not need \\(x\\), \\(y\\) and \\(z\\) one by one — only their sum, and it is given."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-285","stem":"\\(\\sqrt[4]{{5}^{6}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\sqrt[4]{5}\\)","\\(5\\,\\sqrt{5}\\)","\\({5}^{2}\\)","\\(\\sqrt{5}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["\\(\\sqrt[4]{5^6}=5^{\\frac64}=5^{\\frac32}=5^1\\cdot5^{\\frac12}=5\\sqrt5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-286","stem":"Given:\n\\(\\begin{cases} x>0 \\\\ \\sqrt{48x}=\\sqrt3\\cdot x \\end{cases}\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(\\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(4\\)","\\(16\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["Square both sides: \\(48x=3x^2\\).","Since \\(x>0\\), divide by \\(3x\\): \\(16=x\\).","Check: \\(\\sqrt{48\\cdot16}=\\sqrt{256\\cdot3}=16\\sqrt3\\) and \\(\\sqrt3\\cdot16=16\\sqrt3\\) ✓."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-281","stem":"Given: \\({3}^{x} \\cdot  {4}^{x} \\cdot  {5}^{x} = \\sqrt[3]{60}\\)\n\\(x = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Same exponent, so multiply the bases: \\(3^x\\cdot4^x\\cdot5^x=(3\\cdot4\\cdot5)^x=60^x\\).","\\(\\sqrt[3]{60}=60^{\\frac13}\\). Equal bases, so \\(x=\\frac13\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-11","stem":"\\(\\frac{5^{n+1}-5^n}{4}=?\\)","choices":["\\(5\\)","\\(5^n\\)","\\(5^{n-1}\\)","\\(\\frac54\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Take out the smallest power: \\(5^{n+1}-5^n=5^n(5-1)=4\\cdot5^n\\).","\\(\\frac{4\\cdot5^n}{4}=5^n\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-09","stem":"Given: \\(\\sqrt{x+30}=x\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(-5\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(-5\\) or \\(6\\)","\\(5\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Square both sides: \\(x+30=x^2\\), so \\(x^2-x-30=0\\) and \\((x-6)(x+5)=0\\): \\(x=6\\) or \\(x=-5\\).","Check: \\(x=6\\): \\(\\sqrt{36}=6\\) ✓. \\(x=-5\\): \\(\\sqrt{25}=5\\ne-5\\) ✗ (fake solution).","Only \\(x=6\\). Trying the choices gives the same result: \\(5\\) fails too (\\(\\sqrt{35}\\ne5\\))."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-10","stem":"Given: \\(x\\sqrt3=\\sqrt{3x}\\). Which of the following gives all the possible values of \\(x\\)?","choices":["\\(1\\) only","\\(0\\) only","\\(0\\) or \\(1\\)","\\(3\\) only"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Square both sides: \\(3x^2=3x\\), so \\(x^2=x\\).","\\(x\\ne0\\) is NOT given, so do not divide by \\(x\\). Factor: \\(x^2-x=0\\), \\(x(x-1)=0\\): \\(x=0\\) or \\(x=1\\).","Check: \\(x=0\\): \\(0=\\sqrt0\\) ✓. \\(x=1\\): \\(\\sqrt3=\\sqrt3\\) ✓. Both work."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-12","stem":"Given: \\(2^x+2^x=4^x\\)\n\\(x=?\\)","choices":["\\(0\\)","\\(1\\)","\\(2\\)","Every number \\(x\\) satisfies the equation."],"correct":1,"explanation":["Left side: \\(2^x+2^x=2\\cdot2^x=2^{x+1}\\). Right side: \\(4^x=2^{2x}\\).","Equal exponents: \\(x+1=2x\\), so \\(x=1\\).","Check: \\(2+2=4=4^1\\) ✓. With \\(x=2\\): \\(4+4=8\\ne16\\), so choice (4) is the trap \\(2^x+2^x=4^x\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-r26-t10-16","stem":"Given: \\(3^{20}+3^{20}+3^{20}=9^n\\)\n\\(n=?\\)","choices":["\\(10\\)","\\(10.5\\)","\\(21\\)","\\(30\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Left side: \\(3\\cdot3^{20}=3^{21}\\). Right side: \\(9^n=(3^2)^n=3^{2n}\\).","Equal exponents: \\(2n=21\\), so \\(n=10.5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-284","stem":"The numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are such that \\(x^a\\cdot x^b=x^{ab}\\) for every \\(x>1\\). Which of the following is necessarily true?","choices":["\\(a + b = 0\\)","\\(a \\cdot  b = a + b\\)","\\({a}^{b} = a + b\\)","None of the above is necessarily true."],"correct":1,"explanation":["Same base: \\(x^a\\cdot x^b=x^{a+b}\\) always.","This equals \\(x^{ab}\\) for every \\(x>1\\), so the exponents are equal: \\(a+b=ab\\).","Choices (1) and (3) are not necessarily true. For example, \\(a=3\\) and \\(b=\\frac32\\): \\(a+b=ab=4.5\\), but \\(a+b\\ne0\\) and \\(3^{1.5}\\approx5.2\\ne4.5\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-287","stem":"Dana says: \\(7>\\sqrt5+\\sqrt{20}\\).\nYoav says: \\(4\\sqrt3>5\\sqrt2\\).\nWhich of the following is correct?","choices":["Only Dana is right.","Only Yoav is right.","Both are wrong.","Both are right."],"correct":0,"explanation":["Dana: \\(\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt5\\), so \\(\\sqrt5+\\sqrt{20}=3\\sqrt5\\). Square both: \\((3\\sqrt5)^2=45\\) and \\(7^2=49\\). Since \\(45<49\\), Dana is right.","Yoav: square both: \\((4\\sqrt3)^2=48\\) and \\((5\\sqrt2)^2=50\\). Since \\(48<50\\), \\(4\\sqrt3<5\\sqrt2\\) and Yoav is wrong.","Only Dana is right."]}]}],"passages":{}}